    <string name="about_application_title">Application</string>
    <string name="about_description">Light is an app for viewing power outage schedules in Ukraine. Save your home, work, and other important locations to see today’s and tomorrow’s schedules and plan your day.</string>
    <string name="about_how_it_works_title">How it works</string>
    <string name="about_how_it_works_body">Add a location: select your region, electricity provider, and outage group. Choose a name and icon. The home screen shows a schedule with half-hour intervals, a current time marker, and the last update time. All schedules use Kyiv time.</string>
    <string name="about_reminders_title">Reminders</string>
    <string name="about_reminders_body">For each location, choose how many minutes before an outage to receive a reminder. The “Do not disturb at night” option silences reminders from 23:00 to 07:00. Allow notifications in Android settings. Delivery time depends on system permissions and device restrictions.</string>
    <string name="about_widget_title">Widget and offline access</string>
    <string name="about_widget_body">Add a home screen widget to view the schedule without opening the app and switch between today and tomorrow. Downloaded schedules are saved on your device and remain available offline. An internet connection is required to get fresh data.</string>
    <string name="about_sources_title">Data sources</string>
    <string name="about_sources_body">The app downloads published schedules from the YASNO API and open outage data repositories. Tomorrow’s schedule appears after the source publishes it. Accuracy depends on these sources, and saved data may become outdated. During emergency outages, the actual power supply may differ from the schedule.</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_body">Saved locations and settings are stored locally on your device. The app uses Firebase for usage analytics, crash reports, and service messages. Saved location names are not added to analytics events or crash reports.</string>
